<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $409.6 mln Nov 25.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $409.6 mln Nov 25.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $409.6 million surplus on Nov 25 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>Dealers said dollars inflows to pay for shares of Rio de Janeiro power utility Cerj, which was privatized last Wednesday, continued on Monday.  </p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 25</p>
<p>Exports: $171 million</p>
<p>Imports: $215 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $608.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $154.8 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $409.6 million</p>
<p>NOVEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.849 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.068 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $6.577 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.985 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $2.373 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511-2485418</p>
</text>
